{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"65310feb8e1ad07f","name":"card_event_on_the_horizon","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Japan/BrothersInArms/events/card_event_on_the_horizon","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"ON THE HORIZON","text":"This turn, your units are immune to damage and have \"Cannot attack the enemy HQ.\"","flavorText":"At the start of WWII the Imperial Japanese Navy (IJN), held a significant advantage over the Allied navies in the Pacific. They had a larger number of battleships, including the Yamato and Musashi, which were the largest ever built. The Japanese Navy also possessed more aircraft carriers, such as the Akagi and Kaga, and had a well-trained naval aviation force. Their submarines were effective in offensive operations. However, as the war progressed, the Allied navies, particularly the United States Navy, improved their capabilities and eventually gained the upper hand. The Battle of Midway marked a turning point where the U.S. Navy dealt a severe blow to the Japanese carrier force. Despite the initial advantage, the Japanese Navy faced increasing challenges from the growing strength of the Allies.","faction":"Japan","type":"order","rarity":"Rare","cost":1,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_on_the_horizon","title":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_on_the_horizon_title","SourceString":"ON THE HORIZON","LocalizedString":"ON THE HORIZON"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Japan","kredits":1,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_on_the_horizon_text","SourceString":"This turn, your units are immune to damage and have \"Cannot attack the enemy HQ.\"","LocalizedString":"This turn, your units are immune to damage and have \"Cannot attack the enemy HQ.\""},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_on_the_horizon_history","SourceString":"At the start of WWII the Imperial Japanese Navy (IJN), held a significant 